description:
Owner 2026-10-30, asking how MUDs do it, quoted: "should every mob have health but have a flag that says unattackable or something?"; then approved the PM rec, quoted: "yes file it that way". Planned for a later session (not today).
Model (Diku-family convention): every NPC has hp by default; protection is authored, not a data gap:
- an NPC flag "can't be attacked" (name in the plan) and a room flag "peaceful" (no combat starts there);
- both produce the same unavailable reason and refusal loka-xyyd adds ("can't be hurt", reasons.ts sentence), so xyyd's work carries over;
- content can switch them in play (e.g. a guard becomes attackable while the player is wanted; protection ends after a quest), via existing reaction/fact machinery;
- condition sentences, healing and poison then work for every NPC.
Then retire "no hp means can't be hurt" (loka-ysbt ruling, loka-xyyd) as compatibility-only. Engine + schema + content: needs a composition record and plan before a brief (docs/system/architecture.md#building-mechanics-by-composition). Showcase: a peaceful inn and a protected shopkeeper. Every feature ships a story.
